      "message": "\u003e Hi eric\n\u003e \n\u003e I have a same issue with you where use bpftrace. I found Google have fix this by \n\u003e \n\u003e https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20230420010029.2702543-1-elsk@google.com/ and merged with https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2635289, \n\u003e \n\u003e but it doesn\u0027t fix the issue. I don\u0027t know why not fix tar 😂\n\u003e \n\u003e Brs,\n\u003e Hailong.\n\noh, same fix :), but not ported on android-14 kernel-6.1:\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20230420010029.2702543-1-elsk@google.com\n\nThere\u0027s no need to add #include \u003cxx.h\u003e in .bt when using bpftrace if kernel supports BTF(CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF\u003dy), also, headers can be wrapped by BPFTRACE_HAVE_BTF, e.g.:\n\n#ifndef BPFTRACE_HAVE_BTF\n#include \u003clinux/xxx.h\u003e\n#endif",
